{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":504231,"name":"Keil","username":"KeilMS","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/k/9e8a1a/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-30T19:48:47.204Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504231-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504231-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504231-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504231-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExisting support ticket: T-G14112. It has been open for a while with no useful action.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot’s cloud computer will not stay up. Platform restore keeps copying ~117GB back into home/box/Projects and fills the disk, so the computer fails to boot. The computer is stuck in a reset/update loop that never works. This issue persist after more than a week of contacting support. Grok Bot is unusable.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSupport already grew the disk from 126GB to 252GB. That did not fix it. The next restore still brings Projects back and fills the disk again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ehome/box/Projects is a SharePoint mirror. The real files already live in SharePoint. They do not need to be restored onto this computer for the bots to work.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease rebuild this account’s Grok Bot computer on the backend and skip restoring home/box/Projects (or provision a clean computer with no restore of that tree).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease do not Reset from the app in a way that drops existing Bots, chats, routines, files, or logins. Please do not tell me to delete the Cursor account. This account has SuperGrok linked. I need the same account kept.\u003cbr\u003e\nAgents are able to reply via grok app online but not the grok bot app on IOS. Likely requires the virtual machine to be up for messaging through the grok bot app on IOS.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504231-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504231-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eComputer becomes unreachable / will not boot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePlatform restore runs and copies ~117GB into home/box/Projects.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDisk fills. Computer fails again.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDisk was grown 126GB → 252GB. Same restore loop.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTicket T-G14112 opened. Still waiting on a backend rebuild that skips Projects.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504231-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504231-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA reachable Grok Bot computer on this same account.\u003cbr\u003e\nBots, chats, routines, files, and logins kept.\u003cbr\u003e\nhome/box/Projects not restored from the broken disk image.\u003cbr\u003e\nSharePoint remains the source of truth for project files.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-504231-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-504231-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/b/9/b9892bce99d6413f71dc974c496721144b68ef4d.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/qtkdCVFgpSIEGsBgjdwCWEeKMQ5.png?dl=1\" title=\"Screenshot 2026-09-30 124441.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/b/9/b9892bce99d6413f71dc974c496721144b68ef4d_2_690x497.png\" alt=\"Sc